{# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Terrakube job-failure alerts.

   Vikunja #3227/#3267a. The Terrakube API/executor container's stdout
   reaches Splunk via the host's journald docker driver as plain syslog —
   there is no dedicated `terrakube` index and no structured job-status
   event (unlike Semaphore's `index=semaphore sourcetype=semaphore:run`
   push). The container is identified by host (the `iac` VM), not by a
   `terrakube` string in the log line — the docker driver logs lines
   prefixed with the container's short hash, so a keyword search for
   "terrakube" across `index=*` misses the app's own logs entirely and
   only catches the ingress layer (Traefik/Authelia access logs).
   Verified live 2026-09-22: `index=os host=iac` carries plain Java stack
   traces at ERROR level for both a real job failure and an orphaned
   Quartz trigger repeatedly throwing `IllegalStateException: Job <id> not
   found` (`org.quartz.core.JobExecutionProcessException`) — the exact
   #3267a symptom.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
[terrakube_job_error_detector]
description = Alerts when the Terrakube API/executor container (host=iac) logs an unhandled job exception — a real job failure or an orphaned Quartz trigger (IllegalStateException: Job <id> not found is the #3267a symptom: a trigger left behind after its job row was deleted, firing every ~30s). Terrakube exposes no structured job-status event today (contrast Semaphore's index=semaphore sourcetype=semaphore:run push) — this reads the container's own ERROR-level stack traces instead. Threshold is a count over the dispatch window so one blip doesn't page; sustained recurrence (an orphaned trigger firing every cycle) crosses it quickly.
search = index=os host=iac sourcetype=syslog ("JobExecutionProcessException" OR "threw an unhandled Exception" OR "threw an exception") | rex "Job (?<quartz_job>DEFAULT\.\S+) threw" | stats count values(quartz_job) as quartz_jobs | where count > 3
dispatch.earliest_time = -15m
dispatch.latest_time = now
cron_schedule = */5 * * * *
enableSched = 1
is_visible = 1
disabled = 0
alert.severity = 3
alert.suppress = 1
alert.suppress.period = 60m
alert.track = 1
counttype = number of events
relation = greater than
quantity = 0
